.TH GEMTEXT2MOM 1 "2026-11-09"
.SH NAME
gemtext2mom \- convert Gemtext to groff mom
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gemtext2mom
.RB [ \-\-style\  \fISTYLE\fP ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-italics ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gemtext2mom
reads Gemtext on standard input and writes a document in the
.BR groff_mom (7)
macro package to standard output.
Format it with
.BR groff (1),
for example with
.BR "groff \-mom \-Tpdf" .
The title of the document is the text of its first heading.
If the document begins with that heading, it appears only as the title;
otherwise it appears as the title and also remains in the text where it
was.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-style\  STYLE
Select the visual style.
.I STYLE
is one of
.BR default ,
.BR sans\-serif
and
.BR cap\-heads ;
the default is
.BR default .
See
.BR STYLES .
.TP
.B \-\-no\-italics
Leave asterisks as they are instead of setting the text between them in
italics.
See
.BR ITALICS .
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print a usage message and exit.
.SH INPUT
The input format is described in
.BR gemtext (7).
.SH STYLES
The following styles are available.
.TP
.B default
Serif text (Times), bold headings, no paragraph indent, slightly less
than a line of space between paragraphs, and indented bulleted lists.
.TP
.B sans-serif
As
.BR default ,
but in a sans-serif font (Helvetica).
.TP
.B cap-heads
As
.BR default ,
but the title and the headings are set in small capitals of normal weight
rather than in bold.
.PP
In every style, running page headers are omitted and page numbers are
printed without surrounding dashes.
.SH ITALICS
Unless
.B \-\-no\-italics
is given, text enclosed in asterisks is set in italics.
The rules for what counts as such text are given in
.BR gemtext2pdf (1).
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
gemtext2mom < page.gmi | groff \-mom \-Tpdf > page.pdf
gemtext2mom \-\-style sans\-serif < page.gmi > page.mom
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
on success, and non-zero if the input is malformed, or if a write or other
error occurs.
A diagnostic is printed to standard error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gemtext (7),
.BR gemtext2md (1),
.BR gemtext2pdf (1),
.BR groff (1),
.BR groff_mom (7)
.SH AUTHOR
Martin Keegan
